Scoped notice for the verify-block attention design adapted from Splash.
See provenance/splash-verify-attention.json for paths and modifications.

Splash — Apache License 2.0
Source: https://github.com/incoai/splash, revision f786bed (read-only clone).
Files read: runtime/metal/kernels/decode/attention_q8.metal,
runtime/metal/kernels/common/paged_attention_tile.h,
runtime/metal/kernels/common/q8_paging.h; context from PR #91 (a85b086,
optional BF16 target KV with shared attention kernels) and PR #141
(151432a, fp32 logits).
Splash ships no NOTICE file; its LICENSE is the unmodified Apache-2.0 text
(copyright line left as the "[yyyy] [name of copyright owner]" template) and
its THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES concern llama.cpp/ggml material that mlx2 does not
use. The full Apache-2.0 text is this repository's LICENSE.

What mlx2 took: the structure of Splash's verify tile (one threadgroup per
KV head and history split covering every query head of the GQA group and
every verify row as one fused M = rows x heads matrix, so int8 K/V is read
once per step; per-row causal limits inside each split; fp32 split partials
(o, max, sum) merged in fixed split order). No Splash source is copied: the
Metal code in src/mlx2/runtime/models/qsdpa_verify_metal.py is written for
mlx2's affine-quantized cache (packed uint32 codes, scale and bias per 64
channels, strided views) with simdgroup_matrix products in place of Splash's
Metal 4 tensor ops.
